@startuml Subscriptions_DomainLayer_ClassDiagram
!include style.iuml
title MindFlow - Subscriptions - Domain Layer Class Diagram

interface IAuditableEntity {
  +CreatedAt : DateTimeOffset?
  +UpdatedAt : DateTimeOffset?
}
class Subscription <<Aggregate Root>> {
  +Id : int
  +UserId : int
  +Plan : string = "freemium"
  +Status : string = "active"
  +StripeCustomerId : string?
  +StripeSubscriptionId : string?
  +CurrentPeriodEnd : DateTimeOffset?
  +CreatedAt : DateTimeOffset?
  +UpdatedAt : DateTimeOffset?
}
class SubscriptionsController <<REST Controller>> {
  +GetPlans() : IActionResult
  +GetMine() : IActionResult
  +SetDemoPlan(plan: string) : IActionResult
  +CreateCheckout() : IActionResult
  +HandleWebhook() : IActionResult
}

Subscription ..|> IAuditableEntity : implements
SubscriptionsController ..> Subscription : "creates and updates 0..1 per user >"

note right of Subscription
  Plan is "freemium" or "premium"; Status is only used as
  "active". One subscription per user (unique UserId, logical
  reference to IAM). CurrentPeriodEnd is stored but never used
  to expire the plan.
end note
note bottom of SubscriptionsController
  All billing logic lives in the controller (no domain service).
  Stripe is called over HTTP. There is no cancel endpoint.
  demo/plan/{plan} changes the plan without paying.
end note
@enduml
